      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function is taking over some of the bounds logic that was previously handled in SkBlurImageFilter. Once the CPU blur is moved to a callback function, the SkBlurImageFilter wouldn\u0027t have as much duplicate logic (other than the 3*sigma outset). \n\nSome of that duplication can hopefully be addressed by the eventual SkBlurEngine that\u0027s always available and has more consistent behavior around identity sigmas and window sizes. I could also see moving a lot of this logic back out of FilterResult and just into the blur image filter if a lot of the high-level resizing logic can be done agnostically there.\n\nThe one case for keeping it all inside Builder is that we want to be able to peel apart the metadata around the underlying the image. I don\u0027t know if FilterResult can expose all of that nicely for the blur filter to handle it, or if we want to keep it internal (like with all the applyX functions).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1319,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 1319,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "f3ca258d465b50fc57bbef5decc805c0a03f6789",
